1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,412
UbiGraph connects a conversation to a real drone mission.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:16,480
The user describes a target and flight settings. Watch the Agent call its planning tools and generate a plan.

3
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:26,868
Next, connect only Crazyflie two. This establishes the link without taking off.

4
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:41,244
The connection result returns to the conversation. The selected aircraft is ready for an execution request.

5
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,700
The user now authorizes the reviewed physical mission.

6
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:04,112
The Agent selects a flight tool and submits the saved plan to the physical backend. The response is generated here,
in the same conversation.

7
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:24,936
The page keeps recording while the aircraft flies. The conversation is on the left. Real flight and the reviewed
route are on the right.

8
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,920
During the mission, the user asks for a final report. The Agent processes that request without starting another
flight.

9
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,584
The physical recording continues at its original speed through the return and landing. The diagram shows the planned
route.

10
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:22,804
Now watch the report generate. It identifies the physical backend and returns the final status, takeoff and landing
checks, and landing telemetry.

11
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:43,716
The report also states what was verified: command sequence completion and landing. Target arrival was not verified,
and no parking measurements were collected.
